# Pinned toolchain versions — the single place to bump.
#
# aeb tags are "later means later" markers, NOT semver promises; pin them so a
# run is reproducible. Override at the shell to test a bump
# (e.g. `AETHER_REF=v0.897.0 aeb .presubmit.ae`).

# ---- Aether engine toolchain ----

# The Aether compiler (`ae`). Tag vX.Y.Z, branch, or commit SHA. The engine
# uses std.xml (offline generator) and std.regex (PCRE2, for isValidNumber).
# Pinned to 0.897.0 — verified 2026-11-07: every core_tests gate on macOS arm64
# and in a full `aeb .presubmit.ae` on cachyos (x86_64 Linux), plus every
# binding whose toolchain was present there (see the commit that moved this
# pin). 0.897.0 is also the floor: nothing between 0.653.0 and it was tested.
# What the engine needs from a newer ae, for whoever wants to lower it with
# evidence:
#   - `--emit=lib` refusing externs without `--with=extern` (core/.build.ae,
#     core/validation.build.ae pass caps("extern"); the composable-build
#     command lines pass --with=extern);
#   - an extern/export declared `-> string` meaning a counted Aether string,
#     so pn_raw_dup and every string-returning pn_embed_* are `-> ptr`;
#   - `list.get` handing back a `ptr` (no implicit string reading), so the
#     engine and generators read string lists with `list.get_string`.
# Install as a consistent set — a get.sh binary install pairs the driver with
# a matching libaether.a.
#
# Raised 0.897.0 -> 0.908.0 (2026-11-11), a TRACKING bump: no new primitive is
# needed, so 0.897.0 stays the lowest ae this engine is known to need (the
# floor is the pin here: bootstrap.sh derives MIN_AE from AETHER_REF). Nothing
# between the two broke the engine, the generators or any binding. Verified on
# the RELEASED ae 0.908.0 + aeb v0.344 + Zig 0.17.1; per-binding results are in the commit that moved this pin.
#
# Raised 0.908.0 -> 0.931.0 (2026-11-20). The engine, generators and bindings
# needed NO change (they already read string lists with `list.get_string`), but
# the floor moves with the pin, because the pinned aeb must: aeb v0.344 and
# older cannot run on 0.931.0 (their own tools fail to compile, E0202), and the
# floor here is the pin (bootstrap.sh derives MIN_AE from AETHER_REF). Verified on
# the RELEASED ae 0.931.0 + the TAGGED aeb v0.348 (private prefix, not a host
# aeb built from main), CachyOS x86_64; per-binding results are in the commit.
# 0.935.0 (2026-11-22): a TRACKING bump from 0.931.0, no new primitive needed and no source
# change. Verified on the released 0.935.0, Linux x86_64 (ae-x64, aeb v0.349 as the runner): core
# build, core_tests .tests and .abi gates exit 0. The python binding could not run there (no venv
# module on that host) and no other binding was re-run.
# 0.936.0 (2026-11-22): a TRACKING bump, no new primitive needed and no source
# change. Verified on the released 0.936.0, Linux x86_64 (ae-x64, aeb main as the
# runner): core build, core_tests .tests and .abi gates exit 0. No binding was re-run.
# 0.939.0 (2026-11-23): a TRACKING bump, no new primitive needed and no source
# change. Verified on the released 0.939.0, Linux x86_64 (ae-x64, aeb main as the
# runner): core build, core_tests .tests and .abi gates exit 0. No binding was re-run.
# 0.941.0 (2026-11-24): a TRACKING bump, no new primitive needed and no source
# change. Verified on the released 0.941.0, Linux x86_64 (ae-x64, aeb v0.348 as the
# runner): core build, core_tests .tests and .abi gates exit 0. No binding was re-run.
# 0.944.0 (2026-11-25): a TRACKING bump, no new primitive needed and no source
# change. 0.942.0-0.944.0 are performance only (runtime actor batching, inline
# std.math scalars, inline slice-view release). Verified on the released 0.944.0, Linux x86_64
# (cachyos, aeb v0.348 as the runner): core build, core_tests .tests and .abi gates exit 0.
# No binding was re-run. The port makes no HTTP requests and sends no actor messages.
# 0.946.0 (2026-11-25): a TRACKING bump, no new primitive needed and no source change.
# Verified on the released 0.946.0, Linux x86_64 (cachyos, aeb as installed there): core build,
# core_tests .tests and .abi gates exit 0. No binding was re-run.
# 0.949.0 (2026-11-28): a TRACKING bump, no new primitive needed and no source change.
# 0.947.0-0.949.0 renamed string.to_double to to_float (64-bit strtod), sandbox-checked
# os.which/os.getcwd and made a wrong-count tuple return E0200; the port uses none of them.
# Verified on the released 0.949.0: core build, core_tests .tests and .abi gates exit 0 on ae-x64 (Linux x86_64) and, for feat/aether-port, on ghostbsd. No binding was re-run.
# 0.951.0 (2026-11-28): a TRACKING bump, no new primitive needed and no source change.
# 0.950.0 only changed the FreeBSD release (links FreeBSD base -lssl -lcrypto -lz) and 0.951.0
# only adds contrib.xmp setters; the port uses neither. Verified on the released 0.951.0: core build,
# core_tests .tests and .abi gates exit 0 on ghostbsd (FreeBSD 15.1 amd64). No binding was re-run.
AETHER_REF=v0.951.0

# The aeb build runner. Tag v0.NNN, branch, or commit SHA. v0.342 — the current
# release, verified with ae 0.897.0 (v0.341 on the full runs above; v0.342 adds
# only the no-marker root fallback below, checked by building core/.build.ae
# from a `git archive` extract with the released v0.342). (Since v0.301 it
# carries the zig-cc fallback: on a box with no gcc/cc/$CC, `aeb <node>.build.ae` fetches a
# pinned zig (0.16.0) into ~/.cache/aeb/zig once, sets AE_CC="zig cc", prints one
# line, and builds — so bootstrap.sh is one command to a green engine build even
# with no system compiler. (Opt out: AEB_NO_ZIG=1.) Floors still apply: >= v0.298
# make-free binary-first installer; >= v0.287 so a .tests.ae node's non-zero
# return reddens the build; >= v0.342 so a `git archive` or GitHub tarball
# extract (no .git/.aeb marker) builds: the project root for module imports
# such as `import core.phonenumber` falls back to the directory aeb runs in.)
#
# Raised v0.342 -> v0.344 (2026-11-11), tracking only (v0.343/v0.344 need nothing
# from us). One aeb defect to know when running nodes one after another in a
# SINGLE target/: the java SDK reads the node's own previous
# jvm_classpath_deps_including_transitive (own_cp, lib/java/module.ae) and appends
# it to the freshly written one, so every re-run of java/.build.ae repeats the
# classes dir (classes:classes:...) and groovy/.tests.ae, which stats that value
# as one directory, fails "Java binding classes are missing". A clean target/
# (or `aeb .presubmit.ae`, which runs the node once) is fine.
#
# Raised v0.344 -> v0.348 (2026-11-20), a FLOOR move: v0.344 and older cannot run
# on 0.931.0 (E0202 in their own tools); v0.348 is the first release that fetches
# and runs on 0.931.0. The java-classpath repeat defect above is unchanged.
AEB_REF=v0.348

# ---- BEAM family (erlang, elixir, gleam bindings) ----
# Floor OTP 27 + Elixir 1.20 (older OTP's escript rejects gleam_stdlib syntax).
OTP_REF=27
ELIXIR_REF=1.20.4

# ---- Other language toolchains (floors the bindings assume) ----
# JVM family (java/kotlin/scala/clojure/groovy): JDK 22+ for the FFM/Panama
#   binding (java.lang.foreign is final in 22). node 18+, go 1.22+ — as each
#   binding's .tests.ae prereqs declare. Zig 0.17.0+ for zig/ (its build.zig
#   uses the 0.17 build API; zig/build.zig.zon minimum_zig_version), verified
#   on 0.17.1 (macOS and, since 2026-11-11, cachyos) and 0.17.0 (cachyos).
